form. Maintenance scheduling, work orders, dispatch, rental tracking, fuel management, asset tracking and financial reporting all live in one system. It integrates telematics from CAT, John Deere, Samsara and Geotab, and layers predictive maintenance on top, so a fleet manager can see machine health, utilisation and cost in one place.</p><p>For a construction, mining, quarry or oil and gas operation that needs to manage the economics and upkeep of an equipment fleet, that breadth is the point, and a lightweight capture tool comes nowhere near it. If equipment management is your problem, Clue is a serious, capable choice. None of that is in doubt.</p>"},{"kind":"default","eyebrow":"The real difference","heading":"Equipment platform, not a capture layer","html":"<p>The difference between Clue and Quickler is not that one is better. It is that they are different categories. Clue manages equipment: machines, maintenance, parts, telematics and fleet economics. Quickler captures one thing well: inspections and compliance records, on site, without an app.</p><p>Clue includes field inspections as one feature inside a large platform, tied to its asset and maintenance model. That is useful when your inspections are all about the machines Clue already tracks. Quickler is a dedicated inspection and compliance capture tool that is not tied to an asset register at all, so it covers any check a firm runs, machine-related or not, and it runs with no app.</p><p>Quickler does not try to replace equipment management. If that is what you need, Clue is the right answer and a capture layer will not stand in for it. Quickler solves the narrower problem of getting the on-site inspection record captured reliably in the first place.</p>"},{"kind":"default","eyebrow":"The alternatives","heading":"Platforms, paper, and WhatsApp","html":"<p><strong>Clue</strong> is the equipment and asset management platform: maintenance, work orders, telematics, rental, fuel, financials. Pick it when you need 