nage an equipment fleet, Clue is the right tool. If you just need the on-site inspection record captured, that is what quickler does, and a firm might use both.</p>"},{"kind":"default","eyebrow":"Scope, install, price","heading":"Direct comparison","html":"<table><thead><tr><th>Tool</th><th>Scope</th><th>App install?</th><th>Pricing model</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Clue</td><td>Construction equipment and asset management</td><td>Yes, login required</td><td>Custom by fleet size, not public</td></tr><tr><td>Paper and spreadsheets</td><td>Anything, badly</td><td>None</td><td>Free, high hidden cost</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Quickler</strong></td><td><strong>Inspection and compliance capture</strong></td><td><strong>No, WhatsApp only</strong></td><td><strong>£20 per active user/mo, dormant users free</strong></td></tr></tbody></table><p>Clue pricing is custom by fleet size and not public. Check their current pricing before deciding. The deciding test is simple: do you need to manage equipment, or just capture inspections reliably on site? If you need to manage machines, maintenance and telematics, Clue is the right category. If you just need the on-site record captured, a WhatsApp-native workflow removes the app barrier because your team already uses WhatsApp. See <a href=\"/pages/simpro-alternative-uk.html\">SimPro alternative UK</a> and <a href=\"/pages/goaudits-alternative-uk.html\">GoAudits alternative UK</a>.</p>"},{"kind":"faq","heading":"Questions, answered","html":"<h3>Is Clue any good?</h3><p>Yes. Clue is a mature construction equipment and asset management platform covering maintenance scheduling, work orders, dispatch, rental, fuel, asset tracking, telematics integrations and financial reporting. If you need to manage an equipment fleet, it is a serious, capable choice. We would not tell you otherwise.</p><h3>What is the difference between Clue and Quickler?</h3><p>They are different categories. Clue is an equipment and asset management platform that manages machines, maintenance, parts, telematics and fleet economics. Quickler is a dedicated, no-app inspection and compliance capture tool that runs in WhatsApp. Quickler does not manage equipment and is not trying to replace Clue.</p><h3>Can Quickler replace Clue?</h3><p>No, and we will say that plainly. If you need asset registers, maintenance scheduling, work orders or telematics, Clue is the right tool and Quickler does not do any of that. Where they touch is inspections: Clue includes field inspections as one feature of a big platform, and Quickler is a dedicated no-app inspection tool. A firm might use Clue for equipment management and Quickler for its wider compliance inspections.</p><h3>Should I switch from Clue to Quickler?</h3><p>Usually not as a straight swap, because they do different things. If you rely on Clue to manage equipment, maintenance and telematics, keep it. Many firms could add Quickler alongside it purely for on-site inspection and compliance capture, so the record gets caught reliably without another app. Quickler has a free tier of 20 reports a month, up to 10 photos per report, no card and no trial clock. Related: <a href=\"/pages/simpro-alternative-uk.html\">SimPro alternative UK</a> and <a href=\"/pages/alternatives.html\">all comparisons</a>.</p>"}],
