  "seoBody": "<h2>Is Clue a good product?</h2><p>Yes. We will say that plainly. Clue is a mature construction equipment and asset management platform. Maintenance scheduling, work orders, dispatch, rental tracking, fuel management, asset tracking, telematics integrations with CAT, John Deere, Samsara and Geotab, predictive maintenance and financial reporting all live in one system. For a construction, mining, quarry or oil and gas operation that needs to manage an equipment fleet, that breadth is the point.</p><p>So the honest reason a firm ends up comparing Clue and Quickler is rarely that Clue is weak. It is that the two are different categories, and some firms searching for one actually need the other.</p><h2>The real difference</h2><p>Clue and Quickler are different categories. Clue manages equipment: machines, maintenance, parts, telematics and fleet economics. Quickler captures one thing well: inspections and compliance records, on site, without an app.</p><p>Clue includes field inspections as one feature inside a large platform, tied to its asset and maintenance model. That is useful when your inspections are all about the machines Clue already tracks. Quickler is a dedicated inspection and compliance capture tool that is not tied to an asset register, so it covers any check a firm runs, machine-related or not, and it runs with no app.</p><p>Quickler does not try to replace equipment management. If that is what you need, Clue is the right answer and a capture layer will not stand in for it.</p><h2>The alternatives</h2><h3>Clue</h3><p>The equipment and asset management platform: maintenance, work orders, telematics, rental, fuel, financials. Pick it when you need to manage machines and their economics, not just inspect them. It is the right category for that job and a lightweight tool comes nowhere near it.</p><h3>Paper and spreadsheets</h3><p>Still common in UK teams. Free, familiar, no training. The records are illegible, unsearchable, and impossible to produce when a client or regulator asks. The cost is not the subscription. It is the liability when the folder cannot be found.</p><h3>Quickler</h3><p>Quickler runs in WhatsApp. There is nothing to install and no login. The inspection or compliance workflow arrives in the worker's existing WhatsApp chat, and they reply to each question as a message, the same way they reply to anything else. Voice notes are transcribed automatically. The core output is a shareable web report and a permanent record, with optional PDF and CSV export.</p><p>Pricing is only for active users: [[price:bundles]]. An active user is someone who completed at least two workflows that month, so you add your whole team and only pay for who actually works. Everything is unlimited on a paid account.</p><p>The honest limitation: Quickler is not equipment management software. It has no asset registers, no maintenance scheduling, no telematics and no work orders. For any of that, Clue is the more complete product. Quickler is built for teams of roughly 1 to 30 doing structured compliance and inspection capture, and it serves care homes, nurseries, schools, estates, cleaning firms and trades, anyone who inspects or keeps records. Rooted in UK compliance, it works anywhere WhatsApp does.</p><h2>Direct comparison</h2><p><strong>Clue:</strong> construction equipment and asset management; app install and login required; custom pricing by fleet size, not public.</p><p><strong>Paper and spreadsheets:</strong> anything, badly; no app; free with a high hidden cost.</p><p><strong>Quickler:</strong> inspection and compliance capture; £20 per active user a month, dormant users free, only pay for who works; WhatsApp only, no install; UK-based, direct founder contact.</p><p>Clue pricing is custom by fleet size and not public. Check their current pricing before deciding.</p><h2>How to choose</h2><p>The deciding test is simple: do you need to manage equipment, or just capture inspections reliably on site?</p><p>If you need to manage machines, maintenance, parts and telematics, Clue is the right category and a capture layer will not replace it.</p><p>If your problem is narrower, that inspections and compliance checks are not being captured reliably because opening an app on site is one step too many, a WhatsApp-native workflow removes the barrier because your team already uses WhatsApp for everything else.</p><p><strong>One thing to check before deciding:</strong> the two are not mutually exclusive. A firm might run Clue for equipment management and Quickler for its wider compliance inspections, so consider whether you need one, the other, or both.</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>Is Clue any good?</h3><p>Yes. Clue is a mature construction equipment and asset management platform covering maintenance scheduling, work orders, dispatch, rental, fuel, asset tracking, telematics integrations and financial reporting. If you need to manage an equipment fleet, it is a serious, capable choice.</p><h3>What is the difference between Clue and Quickler?</h3><p>They are different categories. Clue is an equipment and asset management platform that manages machines, maintenance, parts, telematics and fleet economics. Quickler is a dedicated, no-app inspection and compliance capture tool that runs in WhatsApp. Quickler does not manage equipment and is not trying to replace Clue.</p><h3>Can Quickler replace Clue?</h3><p>No. If you need asset registers, maintenance scheduling, work orders or telematics, Clue is the right tool and Quickler does not do any of that. Where they touch is inspections: Clue includes field inspections as one feature of a big platform, and Quickler is a dedicated no-app inspection tool. A firm might use Clue for equipment management and Quickler for its wider compliance inspections.</p><h3>Should I switch from Clue to Quickler?</h3><p>Usually not as a straight swap, because they do different things. If you rely on Clue to manage equipment, maintenance and telematics, keep it. Many firms could add Quickler alongside it purely for on-site inspection and compliance capture. Quickler has a free tier of 20 reports a month, up to 10 photos per report, no card and no trial clock.</p><h2>Try this in Quickler</h2><p>Start free, no card, no trial clock. Copy and paste this into the workflow description when you sign up at <a href=\"https://app.quickler.co/signup\">app.quickler.co/signup</a>:</p><p><code>Clue alternative for inspection capture. Workflow name: [Your inspection or compliance check name]. Description: Describe the on-site check you need captured. Include: what is being inspected, number of questions, whether photos are required, and what the output looks like. Quickler builds it as a WhatsApp workflow. £20 per active user a month, dormant users free, only pay for who works.</code></p><p>Quickler reads your description and builds the WhatsApp question sequence. Your team answers on site. Report produced automatically.</p><h3>Related guides</h3><ul><li><a href=\"/pages/simpro-alternative-uk.html\">SimPro alternative UK</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/goaudits-alternative-uk.html\">GoAudits alternative UK</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/fleetping-alternative-uk.html\">FleetPing alternative UK</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/alternatives.html\">All comparisons</a></li></ul>",
